---
name: process-retrospective
description: |-
  Retrospective over recent chat sessions: scan transcripts for what the
  boxholder implicitly taught the assistant (corrections, preferences,
  register, recurring asks, context gaps), then integrate the
  observations into the box's belief surfaces — the personality card and
  guide cards — under the evidence model. Authoritative changes (briefing
  corrections, conflicts with user-stated beliefs) become question cards
  instead of direct edits. Every run leaves an audit report in
  store/reviews/retro/ and commits with a Retro-Run trailer.

  The scan precheck exits CHECK_SKIP when no new chat sessions are ready,
  so on quiet days this procedure does no work and invokes no agent.
steps:
  - id: scan
    description: Observe new chat sessions and record observations in the ledger
    precheck:
      shells:
        - |-
          if ! cb retro status --check > /dev/null 2>&1; then
            exit $CHECK_SKIP
          fi
          cb retro status
      whys:
        - |-
          No need to run the observer when no chat session has gone quiet
          since the last run.
    run:
      shells:
        - cb retro scan
    validate:
      shells:
        - |-
          # Phases run under set -e -o pipefail; `|| true` keeps an unmatched
          # glob (ls failing) from aborting instead of falling through.
          latest=$(ls -t store/reviews/retro/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true)
          echo "Latest report: ${latest:-none}"
          [ -n "$latest" ]
      instructions:
        - |-
          A scan that observed sessions writes a run report under
          store/reviews/retro/. No report means every qualifying session
          failed observation — check the scan output.
      whys:
        - The report is the audit trail; integration keys off it.
  - id: integrate
    description: Integrate ledgered observations into personality/guide cards under
      the evidence model
    precheck:
      shells:
        - |-
          latest=$(ls -t store/reviews/retro/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true)
          if [ -z "$latest" ]; then exit $CHECK_SKIP; fi
          if ! grep -q '_Pending integration._' "$latest"; then
            exit $CHECK_SKIP
          fi
          echo "Report to integrate: $latest"
          echo ""
          cat "$latest"
      whys:
        - |-
          Integration only runs when the newest report carries observations
          that haven't been integrated yet (reports with no observations
          finalize themselves at scan time).
      pass-output: true
    run:
      agents:
        - prompt: >-
            You are integrating retrospective observations into this box's
            belief

            surfaces. The precheck output above contains the run report; its

            runId is the report's filename without .md.


            Observations were mined from real chat sessions. Each carries a

            literal quote (evidence), a one-sentence proposal, and a suggested

            sink. Your job is to turn them into belief updates the next agent

            will actually benefit from — honestly weighted, never overstated.


            STEP 1 - READ THE CONTEXT:

            - The full observation ledger (recurrence lives here — the same
              lesson observed across distinct sessions):
            ```

            cat .callback-box/retro/observations.jsonl

            ```

            - The personality card: config/main.personality.card

            - Any guide card an observation targets (sinkRef, or pick the
              obvious guide under config/).

            STEP 2 - APPLY THE EVIDENCE MODEL (these rules are hard limits):

            - New beliefs enter as source: inferred. Confidence by recurrence
              across DISTINCT sessions in the ledger: 1 session = hypothesis,
              2-3 = low, 4+ = medium.
            - medium is the CEILING for inferred beliefs. Never raise an
              inferred belief past medium; promotion beyond that needs the
              boxholder (create a question card instead).
            - NEVER edit or remove a belief whose source is user-stated. If
              evidence conflicts with one, create a question card.
            - NEVER touch speaking-voice, and never edit the briefing card
              directly — a proposed briefing correction becomes a question
              card quoting the evidence.
            - Strengthen an existing matching belief (one confidence notch,
              respecting the ceiling) rather than adding a near-duplicate.
            - Set ref on a belief to the observation's thread card ref when it
              has one (threadRef in the ledger entry).
            - An observation may answer an item in the personality card's
              unresolved: list — if so, resolve it (move the substance into a
              trait/tone entry and drop the unresolved item).
            - Skip observations that are noise on reflection (one-off
              logistics, no durable lesson). Say so in the report — skipping
              is a legitimate action.

            STEP 3 - EDIT THE CARDS:

            - Personality card edits: tone, traits, boxholder relationships,
              unresolved, experiments only. After ANY trait/tone change,
              rewrite the body paragraph to reflect the updated whole (the
              body is what job agents see).
            - Guide card edits: rules, reactions, experiments, per the guide's
              own schema conventions.
            - Question cards go in box/questions/ as .question.card files —
              follow the existing examples in the box; include the evidence
              quote and the proposed change in the body.

            STEP 4 - FINALIZE THE REPORT:

            Edit the run report:

            - Replace the "What I learned" placeholder with 2-4 sentences in
              first person — what you now believe about the boxholder and how
              sure you are. Plain language, no jargon.
            - Replace the "Actions taken" placeholder with one line per
              observation: what you did (card + field edited, confidence set,
              question card created, or skipped-as-noise) and why.

            STEP 5 - COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):

            ```bash

            git add -A && git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'

            Retrospective: <one-line summary of belief changes>


            <bullet list of edits / question cards / skips>


            Created-By: retrospective

            Retro-Run: <runId>

            EOF

            )"

            ```

            Do NOT add Co-Authored-By. Keep the trailers exactly as shown —

            they make retro commits filterable in the history browser.
          max-turns: 40
    validate:
      shells:
        - |-
          latest=$(ls -t store/reviews/retro/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true)
          echo "Checking $latest"
          ! grep -q '_Pending integration._' "$latest"
      instructions:
        - |-
          The run report should have its "What I learned" and "Actions taken"
          sections filled in, the belief edits should be committed with the
          Retro-Run trailer, and the git diff should show only personality/
          guide/question/report changes — never speaking-voice, never the
          briefing card, never a user-stated belief.
      whys:
        - |-
          An unfinalized report means observations were ledgered but never
          became beliefs — the loop silently stops learning.
      severity: review
---
